It is the **primary component** of a computer that executes instructions, performing arithmetic, logical, control, and input/output operations, often called the ''brain'' of the computer.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

- **Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)** — performs arithmetic and logical operations
- **Control Unit (CU)** — directs the operation of the processor and coordinates other components
- **Registers** — small, fast storage locations used to hold data temporarily during processing', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**ROM (Read Only Memory)** is **non-volatile** memory — it retains data even without power, and typically stores firmware/boot instructions that cannot be easily altered.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**Secondary memory** (hard disk, SSD, pen drive) is **non-volatile and used for permanent/long-term storage**, but is slower than primary memory.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**Output devices** are used to **present processed data to the user** (e.g., monitor, printer, speaker).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**Application software** performs specific user-oriented tasks (e.g., MS Word, browsers, banking applications).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

''Cold booting'' refers to starting from a powered-off state, while ''warm booting'' refers to restarting an already running system.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

An **interpreter** translates and executes the program **line by line**, without producing a separate standalone executable file.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**IPv6** uses a **128-bit address** format, providing a vastly larger address space, developed to address the exhaustion of IPv4 addresses.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

HTTPS stands for **HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure**, which adds **SSL/TLS encryption** for secure data transmission, commonly used for banking and e-commerce websites.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

A **worm** is a standalone malicious program that can **self-replicate and spread across networks without any human intervention**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

WAN stands for **Wide Area Network** — a network spanning large geographical areas, such as across cities or countries, with the Internet being the largest WAN.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

Examples include **Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge, and Safari**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

- **IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)** — provides virtualised computing infrastructure (e.g., AWS EC2)
- **PaaS (Platform as a Service)** — provides a platform for developing applications (e.g., Google App Engine)
- **SaaS (Software as a Service)** — provides ready-to-use software applications over the internet (e.g., Gmail, Microsoft 365)', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

DBMS stands for **Database Management System** — software (like MySQL, Oracle, or SQL Server) used to create, manage, and query databases.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

It is used to **create, read, update, and delete (CRUD) data** in relational databases, as well as to manage database structure and access permissions.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

A common example is **Microsoft Excel** (or Google Sheets).', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

The **World Wide Web** is a **service that runs on the internet**, consisting of web pages and hyperlinks accessed through browsers — the Internet is the infrastructure, the Web is one application that uses it.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

It relies on **networked computer systems and card-reading technology** to allow customers to perform banking transactions (withdrawals, balance inquiry, deposits) without a human teller.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

A **byte** consists of **8 bits**, and is the basic unit used to represent a single character of data.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

The decimal equivalent is **10**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

This corresponds to the binary number **11001**.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)** covers a larger area, typically spanning a city, connecting multiple LANs within that metropolitan region.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

It creates a **secure, encrypted connection (''tunnel'') over a public network (like the internet)**, allowing users to access private networks remotely and browse securely while masking their actual IP address.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**Vishing (voice phishing)** is the same type of fraud conducted via **phone calls**, where scammers impersonate bank officials or other authorities to extract sensitive information verbally.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

A **laser printer** is a **non-impact printer** that uses a laser beam and toner to produce high-quality, fast printouts.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

**SSD (Solid State Drive)** stores data on **flash memory chips (no moving parts)**, offering much faster read/write speeds, though traditionally at a higher cost per GB.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

It is **volatile memory**, meaning its contents are lost when the computer''s power is turned off.', '2026-11-14T06:17:56.365Z');

